pcbkit 2

// PCF8574DWR (Texas Instruments): 8-bit quasi-bidirectional I2C I/O expander, 2.5-6 V, addresses
// 0x20-0x27 by A2-A0 (PCF8574A: 0x38-0x3F), open-drain interrupt; the chip of the I2C backpacks of
// character LCDs (SOIC-16 wide)
// Compiled from the part sheet `parts/PCF8574DWR.json` (`parts.create`); status: checked.
// Datasheet: https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/pcf8574.pdf (SCPS068K (July 2001, revised September
// 2024): table 4-1 pin functions (DW, N), 5.1 absolute maximum ratings, 5.3 recommended operating
// conditions, 7.3.3 address reference)
// Pins: TI PCF8574 datasheet SCPS068K, table 4-1 pin functions (DW or N column: 1-3 A0-A2, 4-7
// P0-P3, 8 GND, 9-12 P4-P7, 13 INT, 14 SCL, 15 SDA, 16 VCC), 5.1, 5.3, 7.3.3
// Footprint: the standard package `SOIC-16 wide (DW)`
// This file may be used, changed and shared without conditions, with the board or alone.

// Note: A character LCD (HD44780) backpack wires P0-P7 to RS, RW, E, backlight, D4-D7; check the
// order the library expects.

/// PCF8574DWR — 8-bit quasi-bidirectional I2C I/O expander, 2.5-6 V, addresses 0x20-0x27 by A2-A0
/// (PCF8574A: 0x38-0x3F), open-drain interrupt; the chip of the I2C backpacks of character LCDs
/// (SOIC-16 wide)
